Third-party material
====================

test/vendor/emmet-2.4.11.mjs is the unmodified ES module bundle from the published
emmet 2.4.11 npm archive. It includes @emmetio/abbreviation,
@emmetio/css-abbreviation and @emmetio/scanner. These packages and the Emmet
snippet data use the MIT license reproduced in data/emmet/LICENSE.

data/emmet/{html,css,variables}.json are unmodified upstream files from the
published package's source commit a96c77a84dc4519de695f3a1625011d908dbe9c0.
Package integrity, individual SHA-256 checksums and source locations are
recorded in data/emmet/source.json. Do not substitute files from upstream
HEAD: its snippets differ from the published 2.4.11 package.

Upstream: https://github.com/emmetio/emmet
Package: https://www.npmjs.com/package/emmet/v/2.4.11

emmet2-fuzzy.el and the native markup/stylesheet engines port algorithms from
the same Emmet source. The Latin, Russian and Spanish lorem JSON dictionaries
in data/emmet/lorem/ are also copied unmodified from that source commit.
The bundle and its oracle adapters under test/ are development-only and are
not included in the installed package.

data/css-names.json contains names derived from Microsoft VS Code Custom Data
commit 01df47ad7cc0b140624fc941ff57618c36ed46a1. Its MIT license is reproduced
in data/vscode-custom-data-LICENSE; data/css-source.json records source paths,
checksums and input counts. data/css-overrides.json is authored project behavior
and is never generated from upstream names. test/update-web-data.mjs performs
explicit, pinned updates; it is not included in the installed package.
